# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# The first rule ignores everything. Nothing reaches this public repository
# unless it is explicitly re-included below.
#
# This is deliberate, not paranoia. The working folder this repo lives inside
# also holds copyrighted article PDFs, raw transcripts of real conversations,
# unpublished pre-defense drafts carrying an advisor's written edits, and an
# IPUMS API key. A conventional allow-by-default .gitignore would put every
# one of those a single `git add -A` away from being public and permanent.
#
# To publish a new file, add an explicit `!` line for it. Re-include the
# containing directory first, or git will not descend into it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*

# --- Repository metadata ---------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/requirements.txt
!/.env.example

# --- Analysis code ---------------------------------------------------------
!/03 Analysis and Code/
!/03 Analysis and Code/*.py
!/03 Analysis and Code/nhgis_extract_spec.json

# --- Never, under any circumstances ----------------------------------------
# Redundant (the `*` above already covers these) and kept anyway, so that a
# future edit to the allow-list cannot quietly expose them.
/03 Analysis and Code/.env
**/.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
